'active','AMFHT',NULL,NULL,NULL),(424,'2023-03-23 03:30:37',28,1,NULL,NULL,15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','T7LAP',NULL,NULL,NULL),(425,'2023-03-23 03:30:37',28,1,NULL,NULL,15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','URAQ5',NULL,NULL,NULL),(426,'2023-03-23 03:30:37',28,1,NULL,NULL,15,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','H752N',NULL,NULL,NULL),(427,'2023-03-23 03:30:37',28,1,NULL,NULL,15,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','1AGE5','\n\nIndustry Type : Mining Contractor, Power Generator, Logistic,\n\nManufacturing, Mining Owner, etc\n\nResponsible :\n\nPage | 13 Aswin Setyawan Margono\n\n1) Requirement gathering and preparing the Business Blue Print (BBP)\n\ndocument\n\n2) Setting up connectivity between BW and ECC system (creating RFC\n\nbackground user, ECC source system in BW, etc.).\n\n3) Enhancing BW DataSource to add additional fields required for Legal\n\nConsolidation\n\n4) Developing BW generic DataSource based on ABAP Function Module.\n\n5) Developing BW data flow to load Actual data from module FI-GL, AP, AR,\n\nAA\n\n6) Developing custom BW data flow required for loading Trial Balance from\n\nECC required by BPC Consolidation (eg. conversion of data from Periodic to\n\nYTD, and from Key Figure to Account- based format, etc).\n\n7) Developing BW Process Chain to automate loading of Master &\n\nTransaction data from ECC to BW.\n\n8) Developing BPC Transformation & Conversion files for Master &\n\nTransaction data.\n\n9) Creating BPC Data Manager Package to schedule Master & Transaction\n\ndata load from BW to BPC.\n\n10) Developing BPC Input Schedules & Reports (complex reports are done\n\nusing Excel Macro/VBA Script).\n\n11) Setting up Ownership Percentage and Corporate Group Structure using\n\nBPC Dynamic Hierarchy Editor (DHE)\n\n12) Setting up BPC Journal for manual Consolidation adjustments (Pre & Post\n\nConsol adjustment).\n\n13) Configuration of BPC Script Logic & Business Rules for: Balance Carry-\n\nForward, Currency Conversion)\n\n14) Configuration of Automatic Adjustment Business Rules that includes:\n\nIntercompany Elimination, Consolidation of Investment (COI), Equity in Net\n\nIncome (EQIN), Minority Interest in Net Income (MINI), Minority Interest in\n\nNet Asset (MINA), Goodwill (for External Acquisition), and SNTRESS (for\n\nInternal Acquisition which is for the purpose of Group restructuring), handling\n\nPre and Post Acquisition reserves, handling Fair Value Adjustment (FVA).\n\n15) Setting up BPC Security (User, Team, Task Profile, Member Access Profile).\n\n16) Setting up BPC Work Status to lock data.\n\n17) Setting up Business Process Flow (BPF) as a guided menu for user to\n\nperform all the required activities.\n\n18) Developing BusinessObjects Xcelsius dashboards for Financial Statements\n\n(Balance Sheet & Income Statement), which fetch live data from BPC\n\nApplication.\n\n19) Conducting user training and support.\n\n20) Developing Unit Test script, troubleshooting and fixing problem during UAT\n\n(User Acceptance Testing).\n\nPage | 14 Aswin Setyawan Margono\n\n21) Preparing Functional and Technical specification documents.\n\n22) Post Go-Live support.\n\n','February 2012','December 2012'),(428,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','KCGLK',NULL,NULL,NULL),(429,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','JPGSE',NULL,NULL,NULL),(430,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','MWX12',NULL,NULL,NULL),(431,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','MUKUI',NULL,NULL,NULL),(432,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','PJSL9',NULL,NULL,NULL),(433,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','29S2I',NULL,NULL,NULL),(434,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','D1V1E',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ User requirement gathering, collecting information of required data from ECC, Teradata and other legacy source system\n\nhttp://www.cpm-consultant.com/\nhttp://www.nol.com.sg/\n\nâ¢ BW data modeling design and data staging to be performed\n\nâ¢ Identify and build prototype of BPC reports/input schedules to be used.\n\nâ¢ Writing the business blueprint covering both functional and technical aspects.\n\n','Feb 2013',NULL),(435,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','6ATQN',NULL,NULL,NULL),(436,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','1HG0J',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ Configuration of BW Process Chain for automated loading of master & transaction data from ECC to BW.\n\nâ¢ Collection and transport of related objects in ECC, BW & BPC from Dev to QA & Production.\n\nâ¢ Perform master & transaction data loading from ECC to BW to BPC.\n\nâ¢ BPC & BW Unit Testing, troubleshooting issues and bug-fixing.\n\n','Dec 2012',NULL),(437,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','2DHIN',NULL,NULL,NULL),(438,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','ZLQP2',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ User requirement gathering, to collect information of required data from ECC source system, BW data staging to be performed and BPC reports/input schedules to be developed.\n\nâ¢ Writing the business blueprint covering both functional and technical aspects.\n\nâ¢ Troubleshooting of BPC NW 7.5 problems after installation and its connectivity to BW system.\n\nâ¢ Setting up connectivity between existing BW to BW-for-BPC, and between ECC to existing BW system, it involves: creating RFC background users, creating ECC and BW source systems in BW (BW source system is required for BW-to-BW DataMart), etc.\n\nâ¢ Configuration of BW DataSource for the following BPC Planning Areas: a. Demand & Production Planning, from ECC: CO-PA (for actual sales data), CO-PC\n\n(Material Ledger) and MM-Inventory Management (for actual production data) b. COGS/COGM/Overhead Cost Planning, from ECC: PP (for Multi-Level BOM structure and\n\nusage factor), CO-PC (for Material Ledger with Cost Component split, to get stock quantity, value and Moving Average Price, by Cost Component), CO-OM-CCA (for Overhead Cost & allocation data)\n\nc. Supply Planning, from ECC: MM (for Purchase Order, Goods Receipt and Invoice data) d. HR Planning, from ECC: HR-PCP (for Personnel Cost Planning data) and HR-Payroll e. CAPEX Planning, from ECC: Investment Management (for Appropriation Request data, ie.\n\nplanned future project), Project System (for WBS data, ie. currently on-going project) and FI-AA (for existing asset acquisition & depreciation data)\n\nf. OPEX or Cost Centre Planning, from ECC: CO-OM-CCA (for operational expense by Cost Centre), CO-OM-OPA (for operational expense via Internal Order)\n\ng. Finance & Treasury Planning, from ECC: FI-GL (for GL Trial Balance data used by Finance-IFRS reports, ie. P&L, Balance Sheet & Cash Flow), Treasury-Liquidity Planner (for Direct Cashflow data), CO-PA (for Finance-Management View reports, ie. P&L)\n\nIt covers both standard BI Content and BW Generic DataSources based on ABAP Function Module and Table/View. It also includes BW extraction enhancement to add and populate extra fields with value using CMOD tcode in ECC side.\n\nâ¢ Configuration of custom BW ETL data staging for transformation of data required by BPC (eg. deriving value by master data look-up, conversion from Key Figure to Account-based format, by using ABAP program in BW Start & End Routines), as well as for loading master & transaction data from existing BW to BW-for-BPC (BW DataMart)\n\nâ¢ Configuration of data retraction from BPC back to ECC using both standard SAP BADI retractor object and semi-automated using flat file.\n\nâ¢ Configuration of BW Process Chain for automated loading of master & transaction data from ECC to existing BW and from existing BW to BW-for-BPC (BW DataMart).\n\nâ¢ Creating BPC Transformation & Conversion files for master & transaction data loading using Data Manager Package.\n\nâ¢ Developing BPC Input Schedules & Reports (including a number of enhancements using Excel VBA Script for meeting complex requirement).\n\nâ¢ Developing BPC Script Logic for Overhead Cost Allocation This part is one of the complex areas, where it fetches data from CAPEX (Depreciation Cost), HR (Workforce Cost), OPEX (Operating Supplies, Maintenance Cost, other operational costs collected using Internal Order). All overhead costs are allocated from other Cost Centers to Production Cost Centers based on below as Driver/Tracing Factor for allocating the costs: a. Plan Activity Hours b. Fuel Demand\n\nc. Percentage manually entered\n\nâ¢ Developing BPC BADI for COGS/COGM. This part is the major complexity in the project as it fetches data from all other planning areas (purchasing from Supply, production from Production Planning, sales from Demand Planning, Overhead Cost allocation from Production Cost Center to the Cost Component of product, and lastly calculation of the Moving Average Price), finally the result is transferred to Finance for Financial statement reporting.\n\nâ¢ Creating custom Data Manager Package to run Script Logic & BADI, as well as Package Link (to link multiple DM packages and run it month by month sequentially)\n\nâ¢ Configure Business Rules for Balance Carry-Forward and Account Transformation used in integration of results from all Planning areas to Finance\n\nâ¢ Creating BPF (Business Process Flow)\n\nâ¢ Setting up BPC Security (User, Team, Task Profile, Member Access Profile).\n\nâ¢ Collection and transport of related objects in ECC, BW & BPC from Dev to QA & Production.\n\nâ¢ Conducting user training.\n\nâ¢ Unit Testing, preparation of UAT script, troubleshooting and bug-fixing during UAT (User Acceptance Testing).\n\nâ¢ Writing final functional-technical documentation.\n\nâ¢ Post Go-Live on-site & off-site support\n\n','Nov 2012',NULL),(439,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','N9DTG',NULL,NULL,NULL),(440,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','01K0Y',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ Fixing bugs in both Legal (based on Entity) & Management (based on Profit Center) Consolidation reports.\n\nâ¢ Troubleshoot imbalance amount between Legal & Management Consolidation reports at the source level in ECC & BW.\n\n','Jan 2012',NULL),(441,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','PWT23',NULL,NULL,NULL),(442,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','L09FX',NULL,NULL,NULL),(443,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','O3BVH',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ Developing project plan.\n\nâ¢ User requirement gathering, to collect information of required data from ECC source system, BW data staging to be performed and BPC reports/input schedules to be developed.\n\nâ¢ Writing the business blueprint.\n\nâ¢ Installation and troubleshooting of BPC NW 7.5 and its connectivity to BW system.\n\nâ¢ Setting up connectivity between BW and ECC system (creating RFC background user, ECC source system in BW, etc.).\n\nâ¢ Configuring BW ETL data flow for FI-GL, AP, AR, AA from BI Content, including BW DataSource enhancement to add and populate extra fields with data required for BPC Legal Consolidation purpose, as well as development of BW generic DataSource based on ABAP Function Module.\n\nâ¢ Configuration of custom BW ETL data staging for transformation of data required by BPC Legal Consolidation (eg. conversion of data from Periodic to YTD, and from Key Figure to Account-based format, using ABAP program in BW Start & End Routines).\n\nâ¢ Creating BW Process Chain for automated loading of master & transaction data from ECC to BW.\n\nâ¢ Creating BPC Transformation & Conversion files for master & transaction data.\n\nâ¢ Configuration of BPC Data Manager package to schedule master & transaction data load from BW to BPC.\n\nâ¢ Developing BPC Input Schedules & Reports (including a number of enhancements using Excel VBA Script for meeting complex requirement).\n\nâ¢ Creating BPC Journal for Pre & Post-Consolidation Adjustments.\n\nâ¢ Configuration of BPC Script Logic & Business Rules for Legal Consolidation (to perform processes, such as: Balance Carry-Forward, Currency Conversion, Intercompany Elimination, Consolidation of Investment).\n\nâ¢ Setting up BPC Security (User, Team, Task Profile, Member Access Profile).\n\nâ¢ Configuration of BPC Work Status & Business Process Flow (BPF).\n\nâ¢ Developing BusinessObjects Xcelsius dashboards for Financial Statement (Balance Sheet & Income Statement), which fetch live data from BPC Application.\n\nâ¢ Collection and transport of related objects in ECC, BW & BPC from Dev to QA & Production.\n\nâ¢ Conducting user training and support.\n\nâ¢ Performing and writing Unit Test script, troubleshooting and fixing problem during UAT (User Acceptance Testing).\n\nâ¢ Writing final functional/technical documentation.\n\nâ¢ Post Go-Live support, including the following tasks: a. Conversion of Source System in BW Development without affecting existing data flow from\n\nECC Production to ECC QA, using tcode BDLS. b. Troubleshooting the BW server down issue and found out the root cause was due to\n\ninsufficient partition space to store archived log files. c. Troubleshooting bottleneck in direct-link between BW Production Primary & Secondary\n\nserver. Secondary server functions as HADR (High-Availability Disaster Recovery), and is located in the Disaster Recovery Center (DRC) which mirrors the Primary server and will be up automatically when Primary server is down.\n\n','Dec 2011',NULL),(444,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','AVW8U',NULL,NULL,NULL),(445,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','QYF6I',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ Troubleshoot BW DB Connect issue with lower-case letters that is not supported in field name (it has to be all-uppercase). DB Connect is used to connect to MS SQL Server as BPC back- end database, in order to retract planning data from BPC MS to BW. SQL View is created in MS SQL Server to select records from BPC tables used to store BPC Application data.\n\nâ¢ Troubleshoot BW Process Chain data loading error. Process Chain is used to load data from the real-time, short-term and long-term BPC Application back-end tables (tblWBâ¦, tblFAC2â¦, tblFACTâ¦ tables), and combine it into one BW cube.\n\n','March 2011',NULL),(446,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','QTTLU',NULL,NULL,NULL),(447,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','ZVOCE',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ Analyze and document the current BW configuration & system landscape as follows: a. BW 3.5 system used by Aqua & Robust CBU (Country Business Unit). b. BW 7.0 system used by Dumex CBU.\n\nâ¢ To propose a Roadmap for the Danone Asia BI (hardware & software upgrade, migration of BW objects from BW 3.5 to 7.0), and taking into consideration the migration of Asia BW applications to Montpellier-France data center. Delivery of the project includes: a. The proposed new BW system landscape. b. Template Implementation, Rollout Strategy. c. Technical Infrastructure and Hardware Requirements (including indicative of effort and\n\ncost).\n\n','Feb 2011',NULL),(448,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','B4609',NULL,NULL,NULL),(449,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','RENXV',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ Develop Xcelsius dashboards for the business users to perform analysis on the HPC (High Performance Computer) usage. Dashboard will show summarized, overall information about: a. ','Dec 2010','Jan 2011'),(450,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','3XSGR',NULL,NULL,NULL),(451,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Team Lead',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','77SGU',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ User requirement gathering for creating total 82 reports with the following breakdown: a. For University Deans/Presidents = 22 BEx Analyzer reports (some utilizing Sub Queries,\n\nBEx Web Analyzer version is also provided, which is published to SAP Enterprise Portal) b. For NUS Official Statistics = 39 WebI reports, based on BEx Queries c. To be submitted by NUS to Ministry of Education (MOE) = 19 WebI reports, based on BEx\n\nQueries d. For NUS Office of Resource Planning (ORP), the department responsible for planning and\n\nallocation of the Universityâs financial resources (budgeting) = 1 BEx Analyzer/Web Analyzer report\n\ne. NUS Office of Admission (OAM) Planning report = 1 BEx Analyzer/Web Analyzer report\n\nâ¢ Designing the data model and writing blueprint documentation\n\nâ¢ Creating DataSources to load master and transaction data from Oracle View using DB Connect and Flat File. For hierarchy, the hierarchy structure supplied by user is re-formatted in Excel and loaded as flat file.\n\nâ¢ Creating InfoObject Characteristics and Key Figures, Master Data Characteristics (with Texts, Attributes and Hierarchies), hierarchical master data design (master data used by another master data), as well as utilization of Navigational Attributes, Reference Characteristics and Compounding.\n\nâ¢ Creating InfoCubes and MultiProviders to physically and virtually store the transaction data. Utilizing Data Mart concept (consolidation/multiple layers) to consolidate/merge data from individual cubes.\n\nâ¢ Creating Formula, Read Master Data, Transformation Routines and Start-End Routines in Transformation Rule (BW 7.0) for the Extraction, Transformation and Loading (ETL) process.\n\nâ¢ Creating Queries, including the use of Sub Queries, Structures, Restricted & Calculated Key Figures, Selection & Formula, Exception Aggregation, saved-reusable Filter (for grouping all the authorization variables and use it in all queries), Variables (Characteristic Value, Text and Hierarchy Variables) using processing types: Manual Input, Replacement Path, Authorization and Customer Exit (utilizing ABAP code in CMOD to populate variable default values in variable screen).\n\nâ¢ Creating Universe structures using Universe Designer, based on BEx queries.\n\nâ¢ Creating WebI reports in InfoView (Java Report Panel). WebI Rich Client is also used for faster access, offline version of report, as well as to backup reports as local .WID files). WebI features used namely: Sections-Breaks-Sorts (including Sub & Grand Total, Custom Sort), Formulas and Variables (using WebI powerful function Median and operator ForEach to calculate median, that is difficult to achieve in BEx. Formula is also used to construct a dynamic report title based on report parameters), Drill, Horizontal table (to display the variable values) and Crosstab (to display query results), Free-Standing Cells, Query Filter (using filter type Prompts) and Report Filter (Standard, Quick and Simple).\n\nâ¢ Creating Process Chains to schedule loading of master and transaction data with hierarchical approach (meta chain, process chain inside another process chain). Updating DB Statistics to optimize query performance, and creating Message to send email notification the status of a process in Process Chain (eg. transaction data load status, delete PSA request status).\n\nâ¢ Designing authorization matrix for both BW and BOBJ. Creating BW authorization (PFCG Role and Analysis Authorization) for reporting type of users, as well as BW authorization required for BW-BOBJ integration (Authorization Object S_RFC).\n\nâ¢ Mapping of Windows AD user used in BOBJ to SAP BW user in BOBJ Central Management Console (CMC).\n\nâ¢ Creating BOBJ authorization (User Group, Access Level, Right, and assigning the User Group and Access Level to Application, Universe Connection, Universe, WebI report).\n\nâ¢ Creating Web Templates using Web Application Designer (WAD) 7.0 and publish them to role, for group of reports that are to be shown as Web Analyzer reports in Enterprise Portal.\n\nâ¢ Transporting SAP BW-BOBJ objects from SAP BW-BOBJ Dev to QA and Production systems (for BOBJ, the WebI reports, Universe and Universe Connections are mass-transported using Import Wizard tool, and individual transport using client tools: WebI Rich Client and Universe Designer).\n\nâ¢ Troubleshooting and fixing problem during UAT (User Acceptance Testing).\n\nâ¢ Writing final technical documentation.\n\nâ¢ Conducting user training and support.\n\n','Nov 2009','June 2010'),(452,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','0IGGY',NULL,NULL,NULL),(453,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','WDJOP',NULL,NULL,NULL),(454,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','3F4WM',' Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ User requirement gathering for creating total 9 reports (all in BEx Analyzer or BEx Web Analyzer accessed via SAP Enterprise Portal), with the following breakdown: a. ','Jul 2009',NULL),(455,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','RTJR7',NULL,NULL,NULL),(456,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'Consultant',NULL,'Hewlett-Packard',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','RG76O',' (HP)\n\nConsulting Responsibilities :\n\nâ¢ Developing BI 7.0 report for MM (Material Management) or known as P2P (Procure-to-Pay) module: Purchase Order (PO) Payment Schedule Report. I developed the report from end-to- end, data extraction for master and transaction data was loaded from SAP ECC 6.0 system and flat file (for legacy data from PeopleSoft, the ERP software that StarHub used previously).\n\nâ¢ Data modeling, using both standard BI Content and custom/generic objects for InfoObject Characteristic and Key Figure, DataStore Object (DSO), InfoSet, DataSource (with standard and generic delta load, as well as the extraction enhancement using Append Structure and ABAP User Exit to populate data into the additional fields), InfoPackage (including ABAP Routine for dynamic data selection from last month of previous year to current month of current year), Transformation Rule (including Formula, Transformation Routine and Start Routine), Data Transfer Process (including Filtering).\n\nâ¢ Creating the query using Business Explorer (BEx) Query Designer, including using objects such as: Restricted & Calculated Key Figure, Selection & Formula, Exception Aggregation, Variable (Characteristic Value & Formula Variables with processing type: Manual Input and Replacement Path), Exception, Condition.\n\nâ¢ Checking the query result in BEx Analyzer (Excel), including coding the VBA script in the Workbook to enhance the report, due to the limitation of BI OLAP Engine in handling the accumulated value (cannot be used for further calculation since cumulative is just a display function).\n\nâ¢ Developing the Process Chain hierarchically (using meta chain, process chain inside another process chain), to automate scheduling the data load, including coding ABAP routine in the Process Chain to selectively delete the content of DSO.\n\nâ¢ Transporting all the relevant BI objects from the Development to QA (Quality Assurance) and Production systems.\n\nâ¢ Troubleshooting and fixing problem during UAT (User Acceptance Testing).\n\n','Oct 2008',NULL),(457,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','41MQV',NULL,NULL,NULL),(458,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','I67CP',NULL,NULL,NULL),(459,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,'Microsoft',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','BF5LA',' (including Stored Procedures, User-defined Functions).\n\nIn addition to tutoring in the computer lab session, I was also required to:\n\nâ¢ Test development server (IIS web server and MS SQL Server 2005 database) and the sample applications for students to practice.\n\nâ¢ Provide consultation sessions for students.\n\nâ¢ Participate and contribute in the unitâs online discussion forum.\n\nâ¢ Mark unitâs assignments, final project and exam papers (with the marking guide and standard provided by the lecturer).\n\nNote : Tutor Certificate of Appreciation from Monash University is included in Other Supporting Docs folder\n\nIntegrated e-Solutions ( http://www.ie-solutions.com.au )\n\nWeb Programmer (Casual Job) Apr â07 â Sept â07\n\nIntegrated e-Solutions is a Melbourne-based company, providing web development services, web marketing and web hosting providers. I worked on a casual basis, having job descriptions as below:\n\nâ¢ Developing new web sites.\n\nâ¢ Adding new website features.\n\nâ¢ Modifying and improving old features.\n\nâ¢ Fixing code bugs. In doing the job, I was exposed to the following software and programming languages: PHP, MySQL, Adobe Dreamweaver, Flash+ActionScript, Photoshop, ImageReady, PHP-MySQL based shopping cart (CS-Cart), CMS software (CMS Made Simple), JavaScript, CSS. Below is the list of web sites I worked on: http://www.gealinaonline.com.au\n\nhttp://infotech.monash.edu.au/about/schools/clayton\nhttp://www.ie-solutions.com.au/\nhttp://www.gealinaonline.com.au/\n\nhttp://www.plutonium.com.au http://www.ie-solutions.com.au http://www.poppysthai.com.au\n\nPetra Christian University â Informatics Engineering Department ( http://www.petra.ac.id )\n\nLecturer (Full-time Job) Aug â03 â Jul â05\n\nOnce graduated and obtained my Bachelor degree, I worked as a junior lecturer in my alma mater, Petra Christian University, a private prominent university in Surabaya, which is the second biggest city in Indonesia, and the capital city of East Java province. I taught several subjects namely:\n\nâ¢ Algorithm & Programming (implemented in Borland Delphi and Turbo C++).\n\nâ¢ Computer Architecture (Turbo Assembler).\n\nâ¢ Computer Vision (Microsoft Visual C++).\n\nâ¢ Data Communication (Borland Delphi).\n\nâ¢ Web Development (Adobe Dreamweaver and Flash+ActionScript). In addition to teaching students, I also supervised them on doing their theses, including coding the software and writing the final report. This is the final unit that has to be completed before students graduate from the course. Another similar task that I did was helping students undertake the internship program. This is considered as a compulsory unit that students need to do toward the end of the course, where they are required to work part-time in a company, observing and analysing the information systems used, helping develop new software for that company, and eventually, describing all the work they have done in a written report. The typical software developed by students for their thesis and internship program is a client-server information system software (either Windows or Web-based) developed using Borland Delphi, Microsoft Visual Basic, PHP, ASP, JSP, MySQL, Oracle, Microsoft SQL Server, Microsoft Access, etc.\n\nPetra Christian University â Continuing Education Centre ( http://www.cepetra.com )\n\nIT Trainer (Part-time Job) Aug â03 â Jul â05\n\n--Content is removed to reduce no of pages in resume. Information will be provided upon request.\n\nWeb Developer (Freelance Job) Jan â02 â Jan â08\n\n--Content is removed to reduce no of pages in resume. Information will be provided upon request.\n\nPrivate IT Tutor (Casual Job) Aug â03 â Nov â07\n\n--Content is removed to reduce no of pages in resume. Information will be provided upon request.\n\nPetra Christian University â Library ( http://dewey.petra.ac.id )\n\nWeb Programmer (Part-time Job) Jan â02 â Dec â03\n\n--Content is removed to reduce no of pages in resume. Information will be provided upon request.\n\nhttp://www.plutonium.com.au/\nhttp://www.ie-solutions.com.au/\nhttp://www.poppysthai.com.au/\nhttp://www.petra.ac.id/\nhttp://www.cepetra.com/\nhttp://dewey.petra.ac.id/\n\nPetra Christian University â Informatics Engineering Department ( http://www.petra.ac.id )\n\nTutor & Computer Laboratory Assistant (Part-time Job) Aug â00 â Jun â03\n\n--Content is removed to reduce no of pages in resume. Information will be provided upon request.\n\n','2005',NULL),(460,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,'Microsoft',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','I1DKB',' Access), SAP BW Query, ECC table - Creating report types: Standard, Crosstab, Mailing Label, OLAP - Using Grouping (including Sub-Grand Totalling), Filter, Template - Using Select, Sort (eg. Top N, Bottom N, Top Percentage, Bottom Percentage; also using\n\nSort Control), Section Expert. Using âUnderlay Following Sectionsâ in Section Expert to add scanned image (eg. form) and put it as background image and display the record fields on top of it to show the filled-up form using data from database\n\n- Using Formula (including Custom Functions), SQL Expression, Parameter, Running Total and Special Fields. Some of Special Fields used eg. Print Date, Page Number. Converting field value to barcode format, eg. barcode for Product Code.\n\n- Sub Report (including On-demand Sub Report, which basically is a hyperlink to the subreport placed in main report, instead of directly adding Sub Report into the main report. Passing information from main to sub report using Shared Variable)\n\n- Using OLE object (Static, Embedded, Linked) - Charts (including Map Chart)\n\nâ¢ Creating Dashboard Reporting using Crystal Xcelsius 2008 - Using Chart objects (eg. Line, Pie, Column, Bar, Combination Charts) - Using Container objects (eg. Panel Container, Tab Set) - Using Selector objects (eg. Check Box, Filter, Label Based Menu) - Using Single Value objects (eg. Gauge, Horizontal Slider, Value) - Using Map objects (eg. USA-continental, Europe by Country) - Using Text objects (eg. Input Text Area, Label, Input Text) - Using Other category of objects (eg. Trend Analyzer, Reset Button) - Using Art & Background objects (eg. Background, Image Component) - Using Web Connectivity objects (eg. URL Button, Connection Refresh Button) - Exporting the Visualization to various file format (eg. Adobe Flash, HTML, Adobe PDF,\n\nMicrosoft Outlook, Word and PowerPoint) - Using Additional/Advanced Techniques (eg. Drill-Down Chart, Row Insertion to Destination\n\nCells, Dynamic Visibility, Ignore End Blanks, Alerts) - Using Data Manager for managing external data connections (eg. Using dynamic data\n\noriginating from Flash Variables, XML Data)\n\nâ¢ System Administration using Central Management Console (CMC) - Creating authorization (User, User Group, Access Level, Right, and assigning the User\n\nGroup and Access Level to Application, Universe Connection, Universe, WebI report) - Managing WebI reports, Universes, Universe Connections and Folders\n\nSAP BW 7.0 & 3.5\n\nâ¢ Data Modeling, using both standard BI content and custom/generic objects, such as: - InfoObject Characteristic (including Master Data Attribute, Text and Hierarchy) and Key\n\nFigure (Cumulative & Non-Cumulative), Navigational Attribute, Reference Characteristic, Compounding.\n\n- DataStore Object (DSO), InfoCube (including Aggregates, Compression), InfoSet, MultiProvider. Utilizing consolidation/multiple layers concept to consolidate/combine data from individual InfoProviders.\n\nâ¢ Extraction, Transformation and Loading (ETL), loading of master data (including Master Data Attribute, Text and Hierarchy) and transaction data from multiple source system types, such as: SAP (SAP ECC, R/3, CRM), as well as DB Connect, UD Connect, Flat File, Web Service, including creation of objects such as: - DataSource (standard from BI content and generic, extracting data using Function Module,\n\nDB View/Table), including extraction enhancement using Append Structure and User Exit (ABAP code written in CMOD and BAdI - Business Add-In) to populate data into the additional fields or via LBWE (LO Cockpit) for Logistics application; Use of standard and generic delta load using Calendar Day method.\n\n- InfoPackage (including ABAP Routine for selective data loading). - Transformation Rule (including Read Master Data, Formula, Global-Local Transfer\n\nRoutines and Expert-Start-End-Inverse Routines), as well as the corresponding BW 3.x data flow objects (Transfer Rule, InfoSource, Update Rule).\n\n- DTP (Data Transfer Process), including ABAP Routine for selective data loading, Error DTP\n\n- Other ETL features, such as: Direct Access (using VirtualProvider and DTP for Direct Access), Real-Time Data Acquisition (RDA)\n\nâ¢ Administration, including the following tasks: - Developing the Process Chain to automate scheduling the master and transaction data\n\nload with hierarchical approach (meta chain, process chain inside another process chain) triggered by direct scheduling or event, performance optimization by updating DB Statistics, error monitoring by creating Message to send email notification the status of process chain, as well as enhancement using ABAP program Process Type, eg. to selectively delete the content of a DSO.\n\n- Transporting all the relevant objects from BI or ECC systems, from the Development to QA (Quality Assurance) and Production systems.\n\nâ¢ Authorization, including the following tasks: - Authorization for administrative user using Authorization Object (PFCG) - Authorization for reporting user (data-level security) using old RSSM & new Analysis\n\nAuthorization concepts (RSECADMIN)\n\nâ¢ Other SAP BW features, such as: - Report-to-Report Interface (RRI), to link reports in BEx Excel Analyzer - BEx Web\n\nAnalyzer â ABAP Report - R/3 Transaction â Web Address - BEx Broadcaster - Documents (with Document Classes: Metadata, Master and InfoProvider/Transaction\n\nData), eg. attaching document in a query for further information about how to derive the KPI (Key Performance Indicator), which is the key figures/formulas\n\n- BI Statistics, BI Administration Cockpit - Remodeling, both manual and using Remodeling Toolbox (RSMRT) - Analysis Process Designer (APD) - OLAP Cache - Open Hub Destination - BW Archiving\n\nSAP BW 7.0 & 3.5 Tools\n\nâ¢ Creating Query using BEx (Business Explorer) Query Designer, including creation of objects such as: - Restricted & Calculated Key Figure, Selection & Formula. - Exception Aggregation (including Nested Exception Aggregation technique) - Variables, such as: Characteristic Value (including Variable Offset), Formula, Text,\n\nHierarchy, Hierarchy Node variables; with processing type: Manual Input/Default Value, Replacement Path, Customer Exit (using ABAP code in CMOD), Authorization\n\n- Exception and Condition. - Virtual Characteristic & Key Figure, using ABAP code in CMOD - Structure (both Reusable and Local). - Cell Editor, Formula Collision - Constant Selection - Rule Group - Sub Query (using Characteristic Value variable with processing by Replacement Path and\n\nreplace variable with other Query result)\n\nâ¢ Creating Ad-Hoc Analysis using BEx Analyzer (Excel) / BEx Web Analyzer, apart from checking the result report, I also did the following tasks in Analyzer:\n\n- Enhancement by coding the VBA script in the Workbook of BEx Excel Analyzer, in order to improve the report to meet customerâs special requirement (eg. to overcome the limitation of BI OLAP Engine in handling accumulated value)\n\n- Creating Query View, changing the layout of the result report, to be used further as a Data Provider for Chart Web Item in the BEx Web Application Designer, in which Chart generally has a specific requirement of data layout.\n\nâ¢ Creating Web Template using BEx Web Application Designer (WAD), which at the next stage will be used to display the report in the Enterprise Portal), including creation of objects such as: - Web Items, namely: Analysis, Chart (Column, Bar, Line, Pie Charts, combination of\n\nColumn & Line in one Chart using several series and dual value-axis), Report, Button Group (with Commands, such as: Export Web Application, Open Variable Dialog, etc.), Info Field, Image, etc.\n\n- Data Provider (from Query View, Query, InfoProvider). - Enhancement by editing the XHTML code manually (including adding CSS â Cascading\n\nStyle Sheet).\n\nâ¢ Creating Formatted Report using BEx Report Designer and Dashboard Reporting using Visual Composer 7\n\nSAP Enterprise Portal (EP) 7.0\n\nâ¢ Content Administration, including creation of iView, Page, Workset, Role, Layout --both standard & custom layout, created using SAP NetWeaver Developer Studio (NWDS) 7.0, to be used later on by portal page, NWDS is also used to package that custom layout Portal Application into a Portal Archive (PAR) file.\n\nâ¢ User Administration, including management of User, Role and Group.\n\nâ¢ System Administration, including Object Locking, Upload/Download/Deletion of Portal Archive (PAR) file.\n\nNote : The scope of my knowledge in Enterprise Portal is mainly for the purpose of displaying the BI reports, embedded on a Web Template created beforehand using BEx Web Application Designer.\n\nSAP ABAP\n\nâ¢ Data dictionary maintenance (Domain, Data Element, Database Table, View, Index, Foreign Key, Structure).\n\nâ¢ Report programming, including: Classical List, Selection Screen, ABAP List Viewer (ALV).\n\nâ¢ Transaction processing using Dialog programming techniques (Module Pool, Screen Painter, Screen Elements, Menu Painter).\n\nâ¢ Function Group, Function Module, Subroutine.\n\nâ¢ Custom enhancement using BADI (eg. for SAP BPC functionality enhancement)\n\nâ¢ Procedural & Object-Oriented programming models (ABAP Objects).\n\nâ¢ ABAP Web Dynpro.\n\nâ¢ ABAP Debugger, Error Handling.\n\nSAP ECC 6.0 & R/3 4.6\n\nâ¢ Financial Accounting (FI)\n\nâ¢ Controlling (CO)\n\nâ¢ Material Management (MM)\n\nâ¢ Sales and Distribution (SD)\n\nâ¢ Investment Management (IM) & Project System (PS)\n\nâ¢ Human Resource (HR)\n\nâ¢ Other features, such as: - LSMW (Legacy System Migration Workbench), including the enhancement in LSMW using\n\nuser-defined ABAP routine (eg. I was using it when loading configuration records into SAP MM Customizing (SPRO) using LSMW. Configuration records for Purchase Requisition Release Strategy are automatically generated beforehand in Excel using VBA script).\n\nSAP SOLMAN (Solution Manager)\n\nâ¢ Project documentation (tcode SOLAR01), including: Insert & Delete Document, Check-Out & Check-In Document.\n\nâ¢ Support message & Transport Request (creating Support Message, Change Request, Correction, creating & releasing Transport Request).\n\nOTHER IT SKILLS\n\nâ¢ System Analysis and Design tools - Microsoft Visio (Flowchart), Power Designer (ERD, DFD), Vensim, ARIS\n\nâ¢ Project Management applications - Microsoft Project\n\nâ¢ RDBMS applications - Oracle, Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL, PostgreSQL, Microsoft Access - SQL, PL/SQL, Transact-SQL, Trigger, Stored Procedure, User-Defined Function\n\nâ¢ Operating systems - Microsoft Windows, Linux (Fedora Core, RedHat, Knoppix, Slackware), UNIX\n\nâ¢ Collaboration tools - Lotus Notes, Lotus Sametime, Windows NetMeeting, Cisco WebEx\n\nâ¢ Virtual Machine - VMware (Server & Player), VirtualBox\n\nâ¢ Conceptual Knowledge - Financial Accounting and Accounting Information Systems\n\nâ¢ Windows-based applications - Microsoft Office suite (Microsoft Excel, Word, Access, PowerPoint, FrontPage, Outlook,\n\nPublisher); including Macro and Visual Basic for Application (VBA) script - Adobe Dreamweaver and Flash (including ActionScript) - Adobe Photoshop and ImageReady - Macromedia Director (including Lingo) - MYOB Accounting - Microsoft BizTalk\n\nâ¢ General programming skills - Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) - Subversion (SVN), such as TortoiseSVN\n\n- Code debugging - Exception handling\n\nâ¢ Windows-based programming skills - Pascal, Delphi, Visual Basic, VB.NET, ADO.NET, C++, Microsoft Visual C++, Crystal\n\nReports, QuickReport, ReportBuilder, Prolog, VP Expert\n\nâ¢ Web-based programming & administration skills\n\n- PHP, ASP, ASP.NET (using VB.NET), ADO.NET, XHTML, CSS, JavaScript, VBScript, Java Applet\n\n- XML and related technologies (Namespaces, DTD, XML Schema, XPath, XSLT), RSS - Domain Registration, DNS Service and Web Hosting - Web Services, both conceptual knowledge and implementation (using .NET) - Template Engine (Smarty, FastTemplate) - Custom-built CMS, Free and Open source CMS (CMS Made Simple, Mambo, Dragonfly),\n\nCommercial CMS (CS-Cart) - Open-source, web-based e-Learning System (Moodle) - Open source PHP and JavaScript add-on packages (phpBB, TinyMCE, mm_menu,\n\nFreeTDS, etc.)\n\nâ¢ Server and Computer-Network applications - Web servers (Apache, IIS), FTP, NFS, NIS, Samba, SSH, SSL, DHCP, DNS, SMTP, Proxy\n\nServer, Firewall\n\n','2008',NULL),(461,'2023-03-23 03:30:48',28,1,NULL,NULL,14,'manager',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','I0IZN',' for âSAP BW Implementation for Procure-to-Pay (P2P) and Plan-to- Manage (P2M) Modulesâ project at StarHub Ltd. Note : Reference Letter attached in Appendix C\n\nPhone : +65 8183 7548 Email : jeff.soon@hp.com\n\nMs. Anitha Swaminathan IT Architect - Computer Centre National University of Singapore 2 Engineering Drive 4 Singapore 117584 Relationship : My project manager for âSAP BW-BO Implementation for Registrarâs Officeâ project at National University of Singapore. Note : Reference Letter attached in Appendix C\n\nPhone : +65 6516 2476 Email : cceanith@nus.edu.sg\n\nMr. Ajay Sharma Lead Systems Analyst - Computer Centre National University of Singapore 2 Engineering Drive 4 Singapore 117584 Relationship : My project manager for âSAP BI Implementation for Office of the Deputy President (Research & Technology)â project at National University of Singapore. Note : Reference Letter attached in Appendix C\n\nPhone : +65 6516 6314 Email : ajaysharma@nus.edu.sg\n\nMr. Benedict Yong SAP BW Senior Analyst System Integration Consulting\n\nPhone : +65 9191 9270 Email : benedict.yong@accenture.com\n\nmailto:willy.adipradhana@abm-investama.co.id\nmailto:jeff.soon@hp.com\nmailto:cceanith@nus.edu.sg\nmailto:ajaysharma@nus.edu.sg\nmailto:benedict.yong@accenture.com\n\nAccenture Singapore 250 North Bridge Road #33-00, Raffles City Tower Singapore 179101 Relationship : My ex-colleague in previous company (Hypercube Consulting Pte Ltd.).\n\nDr. Ly-Fie Sugianto Senior Lecturer & Course Director (Master of Business Systems & Master of Business Systems Professional) Clayton School of IT, Monash University Clayton Campus,