 Exit and creating Generic\n\nDataSources (delta- capable).\n\n7) Extensive use of ABAP to perform complex Transformation routines, Start\n\nRoutine, and End Routine (eg. for Currency Translation and Unit Conversion,\n\netc).\n\n8) Developing BW Query using BEx Query Designer and then saving it as a\n\nWorkbook and add some additional Design Items (in Design Mode) using BEx\n\nAnalyzer.\n\n9) Extensive use of RRI (Report-to-Report Interface) used to jump to other\n\nBEx Queries and to R/3 transactions as well.\n\n10) Using Analysis Process Designer (APD) to calculate Stock Value up to\n\nStorage Location level (standard stock InfoCube 0IC_C03 only support stock\n\nvalue at Plant level) and then download the result to DSO.\n\n11) Designing Process Chain for Master and Transaction data (with Metachain\n\nconcept, using Local Process Chain process type).\n\n12) Setting up Authorization, both Standard and Analysis Authorization\n\n13) Developing BI reports that should cover all Business Processes of DAP:\n\na. End-to-end PTS (Purchase to Stock)\n\nb. End-to-end PTO (Purchase to Order) or Back to Back order\n\nc. End-to-end Dropshipment\n\nd. FOC (Free of Charge) Sales eg. for Replacement, Warranty parts, etc. e.\n\nCash Sales\n\nf. Credit and Debit Memo Processing g. Customer Return\n\nh. Return to Supplier\n\ni. Procurement of Direct Expenses j. Procurement of Assets\n\n14) Developing data loading for Master and Transaction data:\n\n- Purchase Info Record\n\n- Source List\n\n- Substitute Material\n\n- BOM (Bill of Material)\n\n- Selling Price\n\n- etc\n\n','December 2009','February 2010'),(875,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','734HR',NULL,NULL,NULL),(876,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','UAILB',NULL,NULL,NULL),(877,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','KLV3L',NULL,NULL,NULL),(878,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','E7Z7A','\n\nPage | 22 Aswin Setyawan Margono\n\nIndustry Type : Government\n\nResponsible :\n\nAn end-to-end (full cycle) development to develop BI reports with tasks such\n\nas:\n\n1) Gathering requirements from end users and preparing Business Blueprint.\n\n2) Conducting end user training.\n\n3) Developing BI reports covering several modules such as.\n\na. SD reports: List of Cancelled Sales Orders, Report on Water Sales, Master\n\nListing of Contracts, Port Dues by Vessel Type, Maritime Welfare Fee\n\nCollections, List of Top ','February 2009','November 2009'),(879,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,'Customers',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','JEJXI',' for Port Dues, etc.\n\nb. MM reports: Summary of Procurement Returns (for GEBIZ & non GEBIZ),\n\netc\n\nc. FI-AR reports: Revenue Analysis by Tariff, List of Credit Memos issued (Year\n\nto Date), etc. d. FI-AP reports: Partial Payments, etc.\n\ne. FI-TR reports: Impairment Values per Fund Manager, etc.\n\nf. PSM-FM reports (Public Sector Management - Funds Management):\n\nInternal Orders - Actual, Commitment, and Budget data (Comparison and\n\nVariance Analysis), etc.\n\n4) Complex Process Chain (with Metachain concept and Alert system).\n\n5) BI Authorization (both Standard and Analysis Authorizations).\n\n6) Developing ABAP interfaces between ECC-BI-BPC servers for transfers of:\n\n- Master data (Profit Center, Cost Center, G/L account, Fixed Asset, Internal\n\nOrder, Statistical Key Figure of Cost Center) with Time-dependent Attribute,\n\nText, Hierarchy, and Hierarchy Interval information\n\n- Transaction data (Internal Orders - Actual, Commitment and Budget data, G/L\n\naccount - Balance, Funds Management in Public Sector Management), which\n\ninvolves the use of BI Retraction as well.\n\n7) Developing ABAP ALV reports: List of Tariff Items, List of Credit Notes (by\n\nMonth/Year), etc.\n\n','10/20/30',NULL),(880,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','7QTU6',NULL,NULL,NULL),(881,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','T8JF4',NULL,NULL,NULL),(882,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','LPKJ1',NULL,NULL,NULL),(883,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,'Consultant',NULL,'Government',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','R46AH','\n\nResponsible :\n\nPage | 23 Aswin Setyawan Margono\n\n1) Automation of Exchange Rates and Global Settings (Factory Calendar,\n\nCurrency, UOM, Fiscal Year Variant) transfers from R/3.\n\n2) Creating custom hierarchy of Purchasing Groups as the company requires a\n\nhierarchical and higher level view of its Purchasing Groups (using characteristic\n\nPurchasing Group Combination: Capital, Material, Spare).\n\n3) Changing data load for reports that were initially done with Full load, some\n\nimproved with Delta load and some with efficient Pseudo Delta and Selective\n\nDeletion.\n\n4) Changing Materials Management - Inventory Balance report (replacing it\n\nwith LO Cockpit: Inventory Management with non-cumulative key figures using\n\nDataSources 2LIS_03_BX, 2LIS_03_BF).\n\n5) Etc.\n\n','December 2008','January 2009'),(884,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','U53QJ',NULL,NULL,NULL),(885,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','ZHULF',NULL,NULL,NULL),(886,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','3KYEN',NULL,NULL,NULL),(887,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,'Consultant',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','BE4X2','\n\nIndustry Type : Chemical\n\nResponsible :\n\n1) Evaluating around 25 business process scenarios in SD module that covers\n\ntasks such as:\n\na. Creating Sales Order, Delivery Order (Picking - Packing - Loading), Post\n\nGoods Issue, Billing Document, Post Incoming Payment, Inter-company Billing\n\n(exchange of goods and services between Company Codes), Maintenance\n\nOrder. Example scenarios are: Monomer Sales, Monomer Pipeline Sales,\n\nSumipex Sales, etc.\n\nb. Creating Customer Master, Material Master, Credit Control Master.\n\nc. Verifying the correctness of related documents generated from sales\n\nprocess, such as: Material document, Accounting document, Controlling\n\ndocument, Profit Center document.\n\nd. etc.\n\n2) Evaluating around 39 business process scenarios in MM module that covers\n\ntasks similar to StarHub MM module (read above). Example scenarios are:\n\nProcurement of Raw Materials (Hydrochloric Acid, Caustic Soda, etc),\n\nProcurement of Sub-Raw Materials (Local Purchases - Stock and Non Stock\n\nitem, Overseas Purchases - Stock item), Procurement of Services for Projects,\n\nProcurement of Expense Items (Safety Equipments or Operating Supplies), etc.\n\n3) Evaluating Authorization based on Authorization Matrix.\n\nPage | 24 Aswin Setyawan Margono\n\n4) Using LSMW to migrate Master data for SD (Pricing Procedure), MM\n\n(Release Procedure), and CO (Cost Center, Activity Type).\n\n','September 2008','November 2008'),(888,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','VH8P1',NULL,NULL,NULL),(889,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','DC29T',NULL,NULL,NULL),(890,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'active','VLWAT',NULL,NULL,NULL),(891,'2023-03-23 03:31:35',28,1,NULL,NULL,20,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ac